what's going on guys this is rob and we  are back again with another installment  of our beyond omega level series where  we break down the most powerful  characters and comics now today we're  talking about a character who a lot of  you saw putting her powers on display in  the mcu the villain of thor ragnarok  hella but of course since this is comics  explained we're looking at the comic  version of hella who was created by stan  lee and jack kirby and first appeared in  journey into mystery number 102 in 1964  and is way more powerful than the movie  version so like most of the characters  that make up the thor mythos in marvel  comics hella was adapted from norse  mythology and like the norse myth she  was based on hella is the daughter of  loki not the loki that currently exists  in the marvel universe but one from a  previous version of aggar that was  destroyed in a cycle of ragnarok but  hella was born in yotenheim the realm of  the giants and her mother is strangely  enough the mother of monsters in norse  mythology now when she gets older odin  appoints hella to be the goddess of the  dead and gives her dominion over health  a realm which is home to the souls of  the dead now even though the name sounds  like it should be a realm of torture  it's really more of just a resting place  and its appearance can be changed to  anything that hella wishes but the realm  of hell also includes valhalla which is  a place of honor for the souls of the  bravest noblest and most heroic  asgardians and is also used to contain  elysium which was the resting place for  angels of heaven although recently  odin's daughter angela was able to usurp  hela's role of that region but the realm  of valhalla although physically located  in hell is not actually under hela's  control but is itself ruled by odin  however hella has tried on more than one  occasion to rest it from his control and  since her introduction into comics hell  has basically been one of the most  frequent adversaries of both thor and  his father odin now the list of hela's  powers is incredibly lengthy as she is  technically a giant because her parents  are both giants she also seems to have a  lot of physical characteristics and  abilities of an asgardian even though  she isn't really as guardian at all at  any rate she possesses enhanced physical  attributes including strength durability  stamina speed and agility hell has been  able to trade punches with thor and has  even been able to knock him off his feet  in battle as for her durability she  survived hits from characters like moon  dragon and beta ray bill without  sustaining any injuries whatsoever now  hella is also highly skilled in combat  having bested some formidable opponents  in combat including thor valkyrie and  angela now hella is made even more  formidable by her weapon of choice than  knight sword which she can access at any  time and which was strong enough to  impale gladiator who himself has an  insane level of durability now the  knight sword was also strong enough to  cut through  exceedingly durable armor and injured  thor so badly that iron man remarked it  was the worst injury he'd ever seen thor  sustain although at that point i don't  think gore had been around gore  definitely tuned up thor more than hella  did but regardless  i love the thor god of thunder run by  jason aaron but hella's powers go way  beyond her physical prowess as she's  also extremely advanced in magical  abilities which she can use in a wide  variety of ways for example she can  channel her mystical energy into  powerful blasts that are capable of  disarming thor from mjolnir hello was  also able to deflect spells from dr  strange during the time that he was the  sorcerer supreme and we're talking about  like the original pre-retcon doctor  strange who could basically do anything  he wanted to he was just so ridiculously  overpowered that he boarded on  omnipotence and had to basically have  his powers reduced just so they could  tell stories about him so the fact that  not only could hell deflect his spells  but could also manipulate them as she  did when she influenced one of his  teleportation spells so that he  unwittingly ended up in hell shows us  that she's able to perform magic at an  exceedingly high level she was also able  to counteract one of mephisto's  enchantments when she reduced the size  of a wall of fire that he'd created on  another occasion hella was able to sense  the presence of loki which is really  impressive considering his whole deal is  basically being able to sneak around and  deceive people but he wasn't really able  to do that with hella hella also uses  her magical abilities to alter the  environment around her which we already  alluded to when discussing how the realm  of hell can be changed at a whimp now  just to get an idea of what she can do  to manipulate the environment around her  she can immerse an area several miles in  diameter in total darkness or she can  create enormous buildings  instantaneously she has caused the realm  of valhalla to tilt spilling out several  souls into health and was able to cast a  spell that would separate valhalla from  asgard where it was once located and  then relocated to help she was also able  to imbue her sword with enough magical  ability to pierce the protective spells  that protect odin while he's in the odin  sleep which if you didn't know odin has  to take a nap every once in a while to  restore his mystical energies and he's  extremely vulnerable in this state so  the asgardians protect him with powerful  enchantments now according to odin's  grandfather hela's sword also would have  been able to cut down idris sill the  world tree that links the nine realms  now since she is a master of death hella  is able to speed up the aging process  and was able to cause balder the brother  of thor to age rapidly as well as bring  thor himself to the point that he almost  died of old age which is really  impressive when you consider that thor  can live for thousands of years she also  displays mastery over souls and was able  to take a part of odin's soul and turn  it into an entity known as infinity that  was able to destroy planets at will so  if ever there was an argument against  hella being beyond omega level that  should basically put an end to it not  only can she steal part of the soul of  odin but she turned it into a  planet-destroying cosmic entity she also  nearly stole the soul of franklin  richards one of marvel's most powerful  reality warpers but of course her spell  was interrupted before she could finish  it now according to hala she perceives  all of space and time simultaneously  because there is no time or space where  death does not hold sway she can also  teleport characters as powerful as thor  balder and loki across realms against  their will and was able to send loki  back in time now as the goddess of death  hella is able to summon and control the  dead that reside within her realm on one  occasion she sent a multitude of the  dead to fight against the hulk and the  ensuing battle lasted for days and she  still had not used up all the souls at  her disposal she was able to bend the  cosmic ghost rider to her will because  as someone who was technically dead she  had complete control over him in  addition to these souls hella also has  other creatures she commands such as  fenris the wolf a large just contingent  of trolls and giant spiders and the  hellhound that guards the gates of a  realm in fact hella's forces have proved  formidable enough to destroy the  valkyries of asgard so yeah the power  level of hella as we saw her in the mcu  isn't really exaggerated at all compared  to her comic book counterpart and in  fact her comic book version is stronger  than the version that you saw in the mcu  just imagine that everything she did in  the marvel cinematic universe amplified  that about 10 times over and that's how  powerful she is in the comics she's on a  whole different level so with that being  said guys we're going to bring this  video to an end make sure you leave a  comment for anybody you want to see  thank you all for watching and i will  catch you all later  peace
 

